%% Fulfillment, delivery, pickup, return, refund, and RTO journey
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Admin as Tenant admin
    participant Customer
    participant API as Tenant commerce API
    participant Order as Order/Fulfillment service
    participant Courier as Courier adapter
    participant Queue as Shipping queue
    participant DB as Tenant PostgreSQL
    participant Refund as Refund service

    Admin->>API: Confirm order and request fulfillment
    API->>Order: Validate state and tenant admin permission
    Order->>DB: Transactionally update order history/inventory
    Order->>Courier: Create shipment outside DB transaction
    Courier-->>Order: Tracking/consignment result
    Order->>DB: Persist shipment and provider event
    Order->>Queue: Schedule polling or notification work

    alt Courier webhook or polling result
        Courier->>API: Signed provider status callback
        API->>Queue: Enqueue normalized tenant shipment job
        Queue->>Order: Apply allowed delivery transition
        Order->>DB: Persist shipment/order status and history
    else Store pickup
        Customer->>API: Schedule or update pickup slot
        API->>Order: Verify customer ownership and order state
        Order->>DB: Persist pickup schedule
        Admin->>API: Mark ready and verify handover OTP/evidence
        API->>DB: Complete pickup transition and audit
    end

    Customer->>API: Request return for eligible order item
    API->>Order: Check policy, window, ownership, and item state
    Order->>DB: Create return case and evidence requirements
    Admin->>API: Review and inspect return
    API->>Order: Apply inspected return transition
    Order->>DB: Persist inspection and inventory disposition

    alt Refund approved
        Admin->>Refund: Create refund with idempotency key
        Refund->>DB: Persist refund intent/result state
        Refund-->>API: Return stable refund status
    else Return-to-origin
        Order->>DB: Persist RTO state and resolution evidence
    end

    Note over Order,DB: State transitions are enforced by the service, not the frontend.
    Note over Refund,DB: Refund retries must not duplicate financial effects.
